+## Progress (2026-10-04)
+
+Ticket 18 is resolved. The maintainer confirmed the six benchmark suites
+(pow2, smooth, rough, batch, realworld, datacheck); exhaustive N=2..4096
+coverage remains with ticket 20. G8 follow-ups remain tickets 37–39.
+
+Validation is in progress. The baseline reproduced a 24.69% Measure loss
+at f32 N=32768 in a full three-process repeat with 1.00% drift. Aligning
+the planning buffer alone did not fix selection: a clean 56-cell focused
+run still has 11 failures, worst 35.98%. Description fixes now report all
+three scratch requirements, identity/Bluestein metadata, actual packed
+leaf decompositions and batch radices. Tests cover every engine, precision,
+direction and ISA cap.
+
+The replacement selector compares candidates against Estimate on shared
+aligned buffers, with alternating rounds, all placements and representative
+batches. Further diagnostics reproduced a large same-plan timing difference
+pointing to execution context or allocation effects. Constructing Estimate before
+candidate enumeration removes the large N=4096 loss in ten replays. A rare
+N=96 mis-selection does not recur in 30 replays after comparisons at three
+buffer-offset triples. A complete 710-cell, three-process attempt has 28
+timing misses, all with matching plans, and is invalid for acceptance due
+to clock excursions. A/A controls independently reproduce row-context bias.
+The clock probe also compiles its four additions into one memory addition.
+Retaining the full timed batch wrapper and correcting the harness are under
+validation. A clean acceptance run remains outstanding; this ticket is open.
+
+Raw runs, failed attempts, source/executable provenance and the
+[method](../../../docs/benchmarks/2026-10-04-mini-ryzen-ticket19-measure/method.md)
+are retained under the ticket 19 benchmark directory.
